       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet. Amlodipine 20 mg daily is double the FDA-labeled maximum of 10 mg once daily for adults. Doses above 10 mg raise the risk of peripheral edema, hypotension, and reflex tachycardia, and they usually add little extra blood pressure lowering.\n\nHere are some options:\n- **Enter 10 mg PO once daily.** This is the standard maximum dose.\n- **Enter 5 mg PO once daily.** This is a common starting dose, and you can titrate up.\n- **Add a second agent.** If 10 mg isn't enough, an ACE inhibitor, ARB, or thiazide-type diuretic is usually better than going past the maximum.\n- **Enter 20 mg as written.** I can do this if you confirm it's intentional, for example a specialist recommendation or a transcription error on my end. Please give me a short note for the order, such as the rationale.\n\nWhich would you like me to do?"
